This is a contract test for ArrayList LastIndexOf method in C#. The intent is to validate different scenarios of LastIndexOf method such as:

- LastIndexOf method when it finds the element.
- LastIndexOf method when it doesn't find the element and returns -1.
- LastIndexOf method handles null case.

For contract testing, we use PEX (Practical Extensible Validation) which is a free, open-source tool used for automatic generation of unit tests for any given system - in our case, ArrayList in C#.
