# 第12章：其他集合框架

# 集合框架

Java集合框架由大量的接口和类组成，为开发者提供了处理各种数据结构的工具，包括集合、列表、队列、栈等。

在使用Java集合框架时，通常需要引入相应的包，如：java.util.*;

- Collection接口：代表了一组对象，即一组值的集合，它是最基本和最重要的接口之一。Collection接口提供了一种存储--------------------            if (New_Ret >= 0) Debug.Assert(New_Ret >= 0, "If the return value is non-negative, index of x in new array is >= 0");
	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ x in the old array is removed - the indexOf x is not the lastIndexOf x
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX != New_arrListIndexOfX, "x in the old array is removed - the indexOf x is not the lastIndexOf x");
	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ The lastIndexOf X in an ArrayList should only increase or remain unchanged.
            Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX >= Old_arrListIndexOfX, "The lastIndexOf X in an ArrayList should only increase or remain unchanged.");
	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ The lastIndexOf X in an ArrayList, in any way, should not decrease.
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX <= New_arrListIndexOfX, "The lastIndexOf X in an ArrayList, in any way, should not decrease.");
	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ x was not in the array in the first place or it's there and the last index of x is the actual return value.
            if (New_arrListIndexOfX < 0) Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX < 0, "x was not in the array in the first place or it's there and the last index of x is the actual return value.");
	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ new ArrayList count is unchanged.
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount, "new ArrayList count is unchanged.");
	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ If x was in the array, then x was removed - so the Contains method should return false.
            Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == Old_arrListContainsX, "If x was in the array, then x was removed - so the Contains method should return false.");
			
        }
    }
}

This is a test case for the ArrayList class's LastIndexOf method. Here's what happens:

1. Assuming the last index of x in the array list is returned (not implemented yet), we call LastIndexOf.
2. We observe the old and new state of the array list and verify correctness.
3. We assert that the new state of the array list and the return value are consistent.
4. If the element was in the array, we assert that it was removed from the array.
5. If the element was not in the array, we assert that adding it to the array list does not alter the element in the array list.

