A: The method you are looking at is a part of the ArrayList class and it is used to get the last occurrence of the specified element in the list. Here is a brief example:

```java
// Create an ArrayList and populate it
ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<Integer>();
list.add(10);
list.add(20);
list.add(30);
list.add(20);
 
// Get the last occurrence of 20
int index = list.lastIndexOf(new Integer(20));
```

In the code above, we create an ArrayList and add 4 integers to it. We then call lastIndexOf on list with 20 as an argument. The lastIndexOf method will return the index of the last occurrence of 20 in the ArrayList, which is 3 in this case.

